<%!--
  The React mount point, and the one place the document's height is pinned.

  `h-full` chains up through `body` and `html` (both `h-full` in
  `layouts/root.html.heex`) to the viewport, and `overflow-hidden` means
  nothing rendered inside the app can grow the document past it. The app
  owns all scrolling: the sidebar's nav and the conversation pane are the
  scroll regions, and there is no page-level scrollbar.

  Heights are percentages of the viewport rather than `100vh` so that
  browser chrome which makes `vh` taller than the *visible* viewport
  cannot reintroduce an overflow either.
--%>
<div id="root" class="h-full overflow-hidden"></div>

